<title>USA: Justice Dept asks for more data on Ascend-Cascade.</title>
<headline>Justice Dept asks for more data on Ascend-Cascade.</headline>
<dateline>ALAMEDA, Calif. 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Department of Justice is asking Ascend Communications Inc and Cascade Communications Corp for more information about their proposed merger agreement, the companies said Thursday.</p>
<p>This second request could delay the completion of the $3.7 billion transaction by at least 20 days, the companies said.</p>
<p>Ascend, a maker of computer networking equipment, agreed in March, to buy Cascade, a rival networking vendor, for about $3.7 billion in stock.</p>
</text>
